WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:02.919
Good morning Hank, it's Wednesday. I have
a zit so big that when I get close to the

00:00:02.919 --> 00:00:07.390
camcorder, my camcorder believes that my zit
is a face. I mean frankly Hank, this zit is

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:11.380
so big that I've begun to wonder whether it's
going to develop self consciousness and because

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.730
of that I've been thinking about conjoined
twins.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:17.810
So Hank, I thought I would one up your top
five video from Monday and give you top six

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:22.790
pairs of conjoined twins in history, which
is actually, not to brag or anything, kind

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:23.790
of a top twelve.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:28.110
Number six, the Biddenden Maids. Mary and
Eliza Chulkhurst were conjoined twins who

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:32.289
left five plots of land when they died to
benefit the poor of their town Biddenden.

00:00:32.289 --> 00:00:37.079
And for the last five hundred years, continuing
up to today, every Easter there's lots of

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:41.230
stuff for the poor people in this town thanks
to Mary and Eliza. In addition to like bread

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:45.399
and cheese and stuff, pensioners and widows
also get Biddenden Cakes which are these like

00:00:45.399 --> 00:00:50.309
massively disgusting biscuits printed with
conjoined twins on them. Like one 19th century

00:00:50.309 --> 00:00:54.219
historian referred to them as "not by any
means tempting". Anyway Hank, let that be

00:00:54.219 --> 00:00:57.440
a lesson to you, if you leave your money to
charity they will print your face on disgusting

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:01.420
biscuits forever but if you leave your money
to your brother, he will spend it.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:06.160
Number five, Giacomo and Giovanni Tocci. Giacomo
and Giovanni were conjoined twins with two

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:09.920
heads, four arms and two legs and like a lot
of conjoined twins, they spent pretty much

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:14.100
their entire childhood on the freak show circuit.
In fact, the Tocci twins spent like five years

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:17.740
touring America during which time Mark Twain
heard about them, which inspired him to write

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:22.229
"Those Extraordinary Twins" and also inspired
indirectly the great novel "Pudd'nhead Wilson".

00:01:22.229 --> 00:01:26.200
So basically without the Tocci twins, Mark
Twain is a lesser novelist. See and people

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:29.719
say that the history of conjoined twindom
is not interesting. Stop looking at my zit!

00:01:29.719 --> 00:01:34.340
Number four, Lori and George Schappell who
are still living and despite sharing 30% of

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:38.920
their brain matter, have very different lives.
Lori works part time at a hospital laundry.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:43.020
George is a professional country singer. By
the way, they are both female - all conjoined

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:46.119
twins are identical. Its like an autonomous
region of John Green.

00:01:46.119 --> 00:01:49.859
Number three, Jodie and Marie - not their
real names. So in 2000, conjoined twins are

00:01:49.859 --> 00:01:53.370
born in the United Kingdom - Jodie and Mary.
Jodie was the stronger of the two twins - her

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:58.030
heart basically pumped for Mary's blood system.
Mary was a separate person, with a separate

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:02.930
brain but she couldn't survive without Jodie.
Doctors determined that both twins would inevitably

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:08.200
die unless they were separated but if they
were separated Mary would die immediately.

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:11.730
Mary and Jodie's parents didn't want them
to be separated but a court ordered the procedure.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:16.550
As expected, Mary died, Jodie survived and,
in fact, is still alive today. And the case

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:20.750
raised all kinds of questions about personhood
and medical ethics, a discussion that I'm

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:22.410
sure will continue in the comments.

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:26.970
Number two, Chang and Eng, the stars of this
great book "God's Fool". Chang and Eng were

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:31.280
the original Siamese twins, they had a crazy
life that started in Thailand and took them

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:35.440
all around the world. They eventually brought
a tobacco plantation in North Carolina, married

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:40.760
sisters and had 21 kids between the two of
them. Like a lot of the non-separated conjoined

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:44.790
twins we're talking about, they had a fascinating
and very rich life, that in some ways was

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:49.140
probably better than it would have been if
they had been born singletons. Which, by the

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:53.150
way Hank, is the word for people who aren't
conjoined like, you know, us and most people.

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:57.120
This takes me to my favourite conjoined twins
of all time, Millie and Christine McKoy, who

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:00.480
were known as "the two-headed Nightingale".
Millie and Christine were born into slavery

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:05.420
in 1851, sold repeatedly, taken away from
their mother, eventually kidnapped by a guy

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:09.510
who toured them around the world while beating
them. They were eventually taken back by one

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:13.360
of their owners and reunited with their biological
mother and the slave owner and his wife taught

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:17.510
Millie and Christine how to speak five languages
and how to sing in perfect harmony, but also

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:21.620
owned them as property and took all their
money. But then when they were 13, the Emancipation

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:25.290
Proclamation, freed them and they went on
to work sideshows with Barnum and Bailey and

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:28.320
made a tonne of money. Certainly, Millie and
Christine were exploited throughout their

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:31.790
lives, but its hard to say their lives would
be better if they had been separated at birth.

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:34.371
And that's really what fascinates me about
conjoined twins. We're so obsessed with the

00:03:34.371 --> 00:03:39.040
idea that unusual anatomies need to be made
normal, that we forget that unusual anatomies

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:43.160
can have many advantages. That's not to say
that conjoinedness is entirely desirable,

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:47.620
just that the reality of conjoinedness, like
most realities, resists simplicity.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:50.960
Lastly Nerdfighters, as I'm sure you are aware,
there have been devastating floods in Queensland,

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:54.310
Australia. There is a link in the doobleydoo
to help people who have been affected by those

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:57.319
floods. Don't Forget To be Awesome. Hank,
I will see you on Friday.

